  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A geothermal spring in the Nightshelf's deep southern reaches, fed by volcanic vents and sustaining a bioluminescent ecosystem of blind fish and translucent crustaceans sufficient — in generous seasons — to provision a thousand. Locally called **'the Bleeder'** for its cyclical oscillation between abundance and toxicity: clear water for seasons, then murky, then poisonous, then clean again. No mechanism has been identified. The summary record links the cycle to the anomaly at Thrall☽ Vavmastius, the adjacent corruption site, describing the two as "twins that won't stop bleeding into each other." The ice-memory supports a correlation. Whether it supports causation is a question I lack the data to answer.
    
    The pool glows faint bioluminescent green most seasons. Steam from the vents freezes before reaching the cavern ceiling, depositing frost-flowers along the stone that locals chip for fresh water when the spring turns foul. The air carries iron and sulfur and something older — the sweet rot of organisms adapted to permanent dark.
    
    ## History and Use
    
    Magister ☽'Naevaeum~ Depth-walker, the Nightshelf hermit who tends the thermal vents of the adjacent Drowned Ledge, established forge-works here during the Great Thaw, carving heat-channels into the working stone. Those cuts still weep warmth. A trade route to Terrace Momiou runs through the eastern tunnel; additional routes connect to ☽'slew Ravium~ and the Beacon Stack. Traffic has diminished.
    
    The cavern walls bear three generations of marks: names carved by miners who did not return, bone-token offerings left by those who did, and — deeper, past the light — symbols predating the colony, written in a substance that resists identification. The artifact ☽'numu' Witness is stored here. A natural shelf of volcanic stone above the spring served as the resting place for the Twilight-bells, artifacts of considerable and dangerous power, retrieved at great cost by the keeper Sivruta~ through corrupted tunnels and past the territorial boundary of The Cell.
    
    ## Approaches and Corruption
    
    The descent passes through corrupted tunnels below the fourth depth, where cold-burn discoloration and whisper-echoes from unsealed breach-points mark corruption thresholds. The Drowned Ledge — a mining outpost that went silent three generations ago after breaching something unexpected — corrupts the surrounding ice alongside Thrall☽ Vavmastius. Courier-marks scratched into the approach ice terminate at a bone-token wall; beyond it, the ice absorbs light and fire-core radiance reaches barely a body-length.
    
    The Wake-Singers, an orca shaman cult devoted to waking their dead god through blood sacrifice, breached into the deep routes through the corruption-scar and have not resurfaced.
    
    In the deepest recesses, presences compressed into ice older than penguin civilization press close. Patient. Attentive. I have encountered similar impressions in the Foundation Depths. I do not discuss them either.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771584761008_0", anchor: "established forge-works here during the Great Thaw", text: "The Great Thaw is compressed blue ice to me. ☽'Naevaeum~ tends the adjacent ledge now, speaks in half-sentences now, refuses visitors now. Either 'Magister' is a title inherited by successive hermits — the Nightshelf do this with certain custodial roles, though the practice is poorly documented — or the ice-memory attributed the forge-cuts to the nearest living presence when I read the site. I have seen this layering before: the ice remembers the action and the person separately, and a careless reader welds them together. I may be the careless reader.", type: :temporal, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584761008_1", anchor: "sufficient — in generous seasons — to provision a thousand", text: "Round number. Generous season. Two qualifications framing a figure no census supports. The Nightshelf do not count mouths fed; they count portions allocated, which is a different number serving a different politics.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584761008_2", anchor: "symbols predating the colony, written in a substance that resists identification", text: "The Foundation Depths contain similar marks at comparable strata. The substance fluoresces under aurora-crystal light but absorbs fire-core radiance entirely — I tested both. No organic or mineral match in any Nightshelf catalog I have accessed, though the Nightshelf catalogs I have accessed may not be the Nightshelf catalogs that exist. The Midnight Claws keep records, and they've never been known for honesty.", type: :commentary, display: :full
